  "notes": "Cash-basis county. The trimmed PDF has only the Statement of Net Position (p1), Statement of Activities (p2), budget schedules and nonmajor combining pages; the governmental funds receipts/disbursements statement is not trimmed. Receipts and disbursements therefore come from the government-wide Statement of Activities - Cash Basis (governmental activities, no transfers shown); beginning/ending cash are beginning/ending net position and total assets (all cash and investments, no liabilities). Roll-forward: 11,283,359 + 16,823,470 - 17,841,805 = 10,265,024. Taxes 9,851,479 split using fund schedules: General 8,972,891 + Inheritance 600,520 + Visitor Promotion 239,009 + 911 Emergency Management 39,059. Fund-level transfers net to zero across funds (General -2,640,682, Road +2,554,682, Inheritance -179,999, Equipment Sinking +89,200, nonmajor net +176,799) and are recorded in detail only. Nonmajor budget schedule (p7) not recorded in detail since the combining statement (pp8-11) is more detailed; nonmajor recorded with Total column (13 funds). General Fund detail is by department (no object breakdown printed), so recorded as not itemized. Major fund schedules show only fund totals for disbursements. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}